```

## Benefits of Same-Origin Pattern

### 1. Eliminates CORS Complexity
- No preflight requests
- No CORS headers needed
- No cross-origin policy violations

### 2. Simplified Cookie Management
- SameSite=Lax works perfectly
- No domain-specific cookie configuration
- Automatic cookie delivery

### 3. Resource Efficiency
- Backend worker not exposed to public internet
- Reduced CPU usage (no CORS processing)
- Better performance on Cloudflare free plan

### 4. Security Benefits
- Backend API hidden from direct access
- Single domain for security policies
- Simplified CSP configuration

## Migration from Cross-Origin

### Before (Cross-Origin Issues)
```typescript
// Complex cross-origin detection
const getBaseURL = () => {
  if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
    const hostname = window.location.hostname;
    if (hostname === 'app.codevibesmatter.com') {
      return 'https://api.codevibesmatter.com';
    }
    // ... more complex logic
  }
};

// CORS configuration needed
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://app.codevibesmatter.com'],
  credentials: true
}));
```

### After (Same-Origin Simplicity)
```typescript
// Simple same-origin
const baseURL = window.location.origin;

// No CORS configuration needed
// Cookies work automatically
```

## Testing Same-Origin Setup

### Verify API Proxy
```bash
curl https://app.codevibesmatter.com/api/health
# Should return: "Server OK"
```

### Verify Authentication
```bash
# Sign in should set cookies on app.codevibesmatter.com domain
curl -c cookies.txt https://app.codevibesmatter.com/api/auth/sign-in

# Subsequent requests should include cookies automatically
curl -b cookies.txt https://app.codevibesmatter.com/api/auth/get-session
```

## Best Practices

1. **Single Domain Strategy:** Use one domain for frontend + API proxy
2. **Internal Backend:** Keep backend worker on workers.dev (internal)
3. **Simple Cookie Config:** Use SameSite=Lax with no domain restriction
4. **Environment Consistency:** Apply same pattern to all environments
5. **Test Same-Origin:** Verify cookies work without CORS headers

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. **Don't expose backend worker publicly** - defeats the purpose
2. **Don't use different domains** - breaks same-origin benefits  
3. **Don't configure CORS** - not needed with same-origin
4. **Don't set cookie domain** - let it default to current domain
5. **Don't use SameSite=None** - Lax works better with same-origin
